Anthropic Developer Updates

What's new in the API this month:

CLAUDE 3.5 SONNET — IMPROVED
The latest version of Claude 3.5 Sonnet shows significant improvements in:
- Multi-step tool use and agentic tasks
- Code generation accuracy (up 12% on SWE-bench)
- Reduced hallucination in long-context tasks

NEW: TOOL USE STREAMING
You can now stream tool use responses, enabling lower latency for agentic workflows.
See the updated docs: docs.anthropic.com/tool-use

PROMPT CACHING UPDATE
Cache TTL has been extended to 1 hour for all Claude models. This can reduce costs by up to 90% on repeated prompts with large context.

NEW PRICING TIER
Batch API pricing is now available for throughput-optimised use cases at 50% discount.

Read the full changelog: docs.anthropic.com/changelog

